About AppDirect 

 Become a digital, global citizen and enable the new generation of digital entrepreneurs around the world. AppDirect offers a subscription commerce platform to sell any product, through any channel, on any device - as a service. We power millions of subscriptions worldwide for organizations. We do this by our values-driven culture—one that enables you to Be Seen, Be Yourself, and Do Your Best Work.

 About DNE Resources, an AppDirect Subsidiary 

 DNE Resources, a business unit of AppDirect, is an award-winning energy management firm helping commercial and industrial organizations spend less, use less, and harm less with the energy they consume. Founded in 2009 and recognized as one of Canada's Best Workplaces since 2015, DNE manages over $250 million in energy spending across all deregulated markets in Canada and the United States. Through energy procurement, efficiency consulting, and sustainability solutions — and now an expanded portfolio of communication and SaaS services through AppDirect — DNE delivers measurable, long-term value to enterprise clients across North America.

 About You 

 You are a consultative sales professional who knows how to build trust with enterprise decision-makers and turn complex problems into compelling solutions. You thrive in a high-accountability environment, take full ownership of your pipeline, and bring both the tenacity to prospect and the polish to close. You are energized by a fast-moving team culture, comfortable navigating multi-stakeholder deals with operations, finance, and procurement leads, and motivated by uncapped earning potential tied directly to your results. You show up with intensity, lead with humility, and never make excuses.

 What you'll do and how you'll have an impact 

- Prospect and close enterprise-level commercial and industrial clients across Canada and the US, positioning DNE's integrated Spend Less, Use Less, Harm Less framework as a long-term energy management partnership;

- Manage both inbound leads generated by DNE's marketing team and BDR team alongside your own outbound pipeline, owning the full sales cycle from first conversation to signed contract;

- Conduct energy consumption and risk profile assessments with clients to develop tailored procurement strategies — identifying demand charge savings opportunities and building smarter budget forecasting plans;

- Present customized energy programs sourced from DNE's trusted supplier network, translating complex rate and distribution structures into clear financial outcomes for enterprise decision-makers;

- Drive upsell and renewal conversations across your book of business, layering in efficiency solutions (energy audits, demand response) and sustainability offerings (RECs, carbon offsets, solar) to deepen client value over time;

